}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2026, "rank": 28, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2026, "rank": 19, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2026, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "aiq", "title": "Fortune AIQ 50", "year": 2025, "rank": 28, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 64, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 30, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 21, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 68, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 31, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": 7, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 64, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 9, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 26, "itemDescription": "Verizon can boast of being the U.S. cell phone carrier with the most subscribers, with about 144 million consumer and business subscribers as of year-end 2022. But revenue grew only slowly last year.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>The company reported total wireless service revenue of more than $74 billion for 2022.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>In April 2023, Verizon reported broadband net additions of 437,000 in the first quarter of 2023\u2013the largest quarterly gain in more than a decade. That helped offset a steady decline in customers for its Fios TV products, as more customers defected from traditional cable television.</li><br />\r\n</ul>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 54, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 23, "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">In early 2021, Verizon bid more than $45 billion in an auction for airwave licenses to accommodate its transition to a higher-speed 5G network. Over the ensuing year, that investment has begun to pay off. CEO Hans Vestberg says customers are embracing 5G faster than they did 4G, with about 25% of Verizon customers using the faster networks as of early 2022. Verizon can charge a premium for those networks, and its profits were up 24% in 2021 versus 2020. (One ongoing speed bump: Rollout of 5G coverage at and near airports was restricted early in 2022 after airlines and regulators expressed concern about potential interference with airplane navigation equipment.) Verizon announced in April 2022 that it was raising its minimum wage to $20 hourly for customer service, retail, and inside sales employees.</span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 45, "itemDescription": "In his third year as CEO, Hans Vestberg continued to do what he promised Verizon\u2019s board he would do when he interviewed for the top job in 2018: focus on 5G wireless. Spending $18 billion in 2020, Verizon doubled the number of cities with its superfast 5G technology to over 60 and added another slower layer of 5G that provided nationwide coverage (even if it was not much faster than 4G). With the speedier version of Verizon's 5G service ranked as the world\u2019s fastest, Apple invited Vestberg on stage to help introduce iPhone 12 models that are compatible with the technology. The carrier also added a partnership with Microsoft\u2019s Azure cloud service to offer connections over its 5G network, following an earlier deal with Amazon. In early May 2021, meanwhile, Verizon took a big step away from being a content provider, selling its media group\u2014which includes the AOL and Yahoo brands\u2014to private equity firm Apollo Global Management."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 20, "itemDescription": "In his third year as CEO, Hans Vestberg continued to do what he promised Verizon\u2019s board he would do when he interviewed for the top job in 2018: focus on 5G wireless. Spending $18 billion in 2020, Verizon doubled the number of cities with its superfast 5G technology to over 60 and added another slower layer of 5G that provided nationwide coverage (even if it was not much faster than 4G). With the speedier version of Verizon's 5G service ranked as the world\u2019s fastest, Apple invited Vestberg on stage to help introduce iPhone 12 models that are compatible with the technology. The carrier also added a partnership with Microsoft\u2019s Azure cloud service to offer connections over its 5G network, following an earlier deal with Amazon. In early May 2021, meanwhile, Verizon took a big step away from being a content provider, selling its media group\u2014which includes the AOL and Yahoo brands\u2014to private equity firm Apollo Global Management."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 44, "itemDescription": "Revenue was steady at Verizon and profits surged 24% as new CEO Hans Vestberg pursued a strategy of building the best 5G wireless network without further diversifying into the entertainment business as rivals AT&amp;T and Comcast have done. (Its Verizon Media unit retains assets from the former AOL and Yahoo, acquired in 2015 and 2017, respectively.) Instead, Vestberg has smartly partnered with others, including Disney, to supply popular shows and movies to the carrier's wireless customers. Verizon also met Vestberg's promise to start 5G service in at least 30 cities by the end in 2019, though in most areas, the coverage was quite limited."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 20, "itemDescription": "Revenue was steady at Verizon and profits surged 24% as new CEO Hans Vestberg pursued a strategy of building the best 5G wireless network without diversifying into the entertainment business, as rivals AT&amp;T and Comcast have done. Instead, Vestberg has smartly partnered with others, including Disney, to supply popular shows and movies to the carrier's wireless customers. Verizon also met Vestberg's promise to start 5G service in at least 30 cities by the end in 2019, though in most areas, the coverage was quite limited."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2019, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 43, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 19, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2018, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, 